{"name":"Roan Rouge","hex":"#885156","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a coat of a dark base color with individual white hairs mixed in.","Made of roan (kind of leather)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal (such as a horse) that has a coat of a dark base color with individual white hairs mixed in.","The color of such an animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roan"},{"term":"rouge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish pink colour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Red or pink makeup to add colour to the cheeks; blusher.","Any reddish pink colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rouge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Roan is a coat color found in many animals, including horses, cattle, antelope, cats and dogs. It is defined generally as an even mixture of white and pigmented hairs that do not \"gray out\" or fade as the animal ages. There are a variety of genetic conditions which produce the colors described as \"roan\" in various species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/BayRoan.jpg/330px-BayRoan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roan_(color)","wikidata":"Q17115897"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Dutch_Draft_Horse_Team.jpg/500px-Dutch_Draft_Horse_Team.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Dutch_Draft_Horse_Team.jpg/1280px-Dutch_Draft_Horse_Team.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Dutch_Draft_Horse_Team.jpg/500px-Dutch_Draft_Horse_Team.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two blue roa